\section{URL enumeration}{

Unlike the SPA-behind-a-private-API portals elsewhere in the family, this
one is an \strong{OpenDataSoft Explore API v2.1} platform — a public, anonymous,
documented REST+JSON service. The whole register lives in a single flat
dataset (\code{projets-environnement-diffusion}, ~5,483 records, ~62 fields
each). Every field is inline in each record, so there is no separate detail
call.

Enumeration uses the EXPORT endpoint
(\verb{GET <base>/exports/json?limit=-1}), which has no offset cap and returns
the full filtered set in one JSON array. Server-side filters are expressed
in ODSQL via the \code{where} parameter: free-text \code{query} becomes
\code{search("<query>")}, \code{theme} / \code{status} / \code{native_type} become equality
clauses, and \code{date_range} becomes a \verb{dc_date >= ... and dc_date <= ...}
window. The stable business key is \code{recordsid} (used as \code{document_id}); the
ODS internal hash (\code{record.id}) is deliberately ignored.
}

\section{Geometry}{

About 1,472 of the ~5,483 records carry a \code{localisation} field — a full
GeoJSON \strong{Feature} (typically a \code{MultiPolygon}) returned inline.
OpenDataSoft always serves WGS84, so the CRS is \strong{EPSG:4326}. When
\code{write_sidecar = TRUE} and a record has a geometry, it is saved next to the
sidecar as \verb{<document_id>.geometry.geojson} (a \code{FeatureCollection} wrapping
the geometry, with the GeoJSON-2008 \code{crs} member naming
\verb{urn:ogc:def:crs:EPSG::4326}). The sidecar carries \code{geometry_path} and
\code{geometry_crs} (\code{"EPSG:4326"}). Records without \code{localisation} leave the
geometry columns \code{NA}.
}

\section{Attachments}{

Each record exposes a \strong{fixed set of typed document fields}, each holding a
single URL. The handler maps the known fields to stable slugs (DE-style
curated map) and emits one \verb{attachment_urls_<slug>} / \verb{local_path_<slug>}
list-column per field that is populated:
\itemize{
\item \code{dc_relation_expertise_etudeimpact} -> \code{etude_impact} (the EIA study PDF).
\item \code{dc_relation_synthesis} -> \code{resume_non_technique} (résumé non technique).
\item \code{dc_relation_expertise_avisae} -> \code{avis_ae} (avis de l'Autorité environnementale).
\item \code{dc_relation_expertise_reponseavisae} -> \code{reponse_avis_ae} (réponse à l'avis AE).
\item \code{dc_relation_officialdocument} -> \code{dossier} (the \verb{*_DCZIP.zip} dossier).
\item \code{dc_relation_decision} -> \code{decision}.
\item \code{dc_relation_assessment} -> \code{assessment}.
\item \code{dc_relation_expertise_autredoc1..3} -> \code{autre_doc_1..3}.
\item \code{dc_relation_expertise_certifbiodiv} -> \code{certif_biodiv}.
}

Only values whose host is \code{sicodei.projets-environnement.gouv.fr} (or that
end in \code{.pdf} / \code{.zip}) are treated as downloadable attachments — many
\verb{dc_relation_*} values point at external préfecture web pages (HTML), which
are kept in extras columns but never enter the attachment columns.
\code{attachment_urls} / \code{local_path} are the deduplicated union of the real
document URLs, as required by the planscanR schema.
